<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Hobyo</h1><p class="st-meta">1878 CE – 1925 CE (approx.) · capital Hobyo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Somali sultanate on the Indian Ocean coast founded by Yusuf Ali Kenadid, which became an Italian protectorate before conquest in 1925.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ali-kenadid">Yusuf Ali Kenadid</a>, a member of the ruling house of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/majeerteen-sultanate">Majeerteen Sultanate</a>, quarrelled with his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boqor-osman-mahamuud">Boqor Osman Mahamuud</a> and left the north. With followers and Hadrami allies he took control of the coastal town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hobyo">Hobyo</a> in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somalia">Somalia</a> and established a sultanate there around 1878.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultan ruled with clan elders over pastoral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> clans, controlling trade through the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hobyo">Hobyo</a>, which exported livestock, hides and gum. In 1888 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ali-kenadid">Yusuf Ali</a> accepted an Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> to secure his position. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-yusuf-kenadid">Osman Yusuf Kenadid</a> created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osmanya">Osmanya script</a> for the Somali language.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-yusuf-kenadid">Ali Yusuf Kenadid</a> refused Italian demands in 1925, and Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-maria-de-vecchi">Cesare De Vecchi's</a> forces occupied the sultanate, annexing it to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>. Its territory is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galmudug">Galmudug</a> region today.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-hobyo.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Hobyo" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: 26oo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Majeerteen_sultanate_flag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1878 CE – 1925 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hobyo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yusuf Ali Kenadid, Ali Yusuf Kenadid</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hobyo Sultanate, Obbia, Sultanate of Obbia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=sultanate-of-hobyo" aria-label="Sultanate of Hobyo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6025 1977 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Hobyo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6345 2233L6413 2045M6345 2233L6259 2357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6413 2045h0M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6345 2233h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6345 2233h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=sultanate-of-hobyo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
